    {
      "id": "dynamic-port-expansion-criteria",
      "type": "markdown",
      "label": "Pass Criteria",
      "position": {"x": 500, "y": -80},
      "width": 600,
      "height": 500,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "ports": [{"id": "root", "label": "root", "direction": "bidirectional", "dataType": "any", "angle": 210}],
      "data": {
        "identity": {"graphId": "dynamic-port-expansion-smoke"},
        "markdown": "# Pass criteria\n\n## Derived handles\n\nThe Article instance has exactly three derived output handles, in manifest order:\n\n1. **Definitions** (`definitions`)\n2. **Applications** (`applications`)\n3. **History** (`history`)\n\nThe permanent authored `root` handle remains intact. Hovering a derived handle displays its section title.\n\n## Drag expansion\n\nDragging **Applications** into open canvas creates one `wikipedia-section` instance and an edge from the originating dynamic handle. The new instance is seeded with the article URL/title/revision and the selected section's id/title/level/order/source locator.\n\n## Isolation\n\nOpening, focusing, or zooming the graph performs no network request. Reopening the graph derives the same stable handle identities without persisting duplicate handles into authored `ports`.\n\n## Current expectation\n\n**Fail until the runtime interprets the declarative dynamic-port contract.**"
      }
    }
  ],
